<Legal title="Privacy" description="What HD Growth Advisory collects through this website, why, and how to have it removed.">
  <p>
    This site is run by Hugh Duffie, trading as HD Growth Advisory, in the United Kingdom. This page explains what I
    collect when you use it, and what I do with it.
  </p>

  <h2>What I collect, and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Guides.</strong> When you ask for a guide I collect your first name, email address and, if you give it,
      your role. I use these to send you the guide and a few follow-up emails about it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Monthly notes.</strong> Your email address, so I can send you one email a month. You confirm the
      sign-up by email first.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Get in touch.</strong> Your first name, email address, brand, Loom link and, if you give it, a rough
      revenue figure. I use these to watch your Loom and reply to you. You are not added to a mailing list.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Values exercise.</strong> Your answers stay in your browser. Nothing is sent to me unless you ask for
      the report by email. If you do, I receive your email address, your top five values, any notes you wrote and
      your theme profile.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Email addresses and the details above are stored in Klaviyo, the email service I use. The site is hosted on
    Cloudflare. Both act as processors on my behalf. I do not sell your details or share them with anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Until you unsubscribe or ask me to delete it. Loom intake details for brands I do not go on to work with are
    deleted within 12 months.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can unsubscribe from any email using the link at the bottom of it. You can also ask me for a copy of what I
    hold about you, or to correct or delete it. If you are unhappy with how I have handled your data, you can
    complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at ico.org.uk.
  </p>
</Legal>
